    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73685" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμοιο-τέλευτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ending alike</i>
			: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὁ.</span>
			<i>the like ending of two or more clauses</i> or <i>verses,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1410b1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.162
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				12.53
			</span></i> (pl.) : <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τέλευτα</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶλα</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.
				<u>Eloc.</u>
				26
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τέλευτον διάνοιαν κατακλίνειν</span>
			<i>end a sentence with</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμοιοτέλ.,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				2.57
			</span></i>.</div>
